{
 "segments": [
  {
   "start": 0.0,
   "end": 1.9,
   "text": "You can scale without a ceiling, right?"
  },
  {
   "start": 2.2,
   "end": 6.86,
   "text": "When you're using conventional loans, it typically caps the number of properties you can buy"
  },
  {
   "start": 6.86,
   "end": 8.02,
   "text": "right around 10."
  },
  {
   "start": 8.28,
   "end": 12.3,
   "text": "I don't know if that's shifted up or down in the past few years, but right around 10"
  },
  {
   "start": 12.3,
   "end": 14.78,
   "text": "is where the banks will no longer lend to you conventionally."
  },
  {
   "start": 15.04,
   "end": 18.92,
   "text": "With DSCR, because they're looking at the property itself, it's not looking at you,"
  },
  {
   "start": 19.0,
   "end": 20.9,
   "text": "so they'll continue lending as long as you find deals."
  },
  {
   "start": 21.48,
   "end": 25.68,
   "text": "DSCR is kind of cool because it allows you to close in your entity's ..."
  }
 ],
